next: PR #43 (plot visual-hierarchy: bolder teal/plum CI markers on both density plots) still open against dev, unmerged. Part 2 of the ADHD-friendly UX plan otherwise not started (matrix-swatch Part 1 already shipped). medci UI enhancement items #9 (interactive plotly density plot) and #10 (bookmarkable state) still parked -- cross the golem escalation trigger. Dark-mode toggle still parked. GitHub Pages container pages (below) are done through screenshots; no open items on that spec. No third app currently planned.
done: 2026-08-04 -- GitHub Pages landing page shipped (PRs #43-45): docs/index.html two-card menu + per-app pages, both apps cross-linked in their About panels. Then upgraded from instant-redirect stubs to real container pages (PRs #46-47): formula (MathJax), a verified worked example (medci via RMediation::medci(), medmc via an actual Monte Carlo simulation matching the app's defaults -- not placeholder numbers), a collapsible citation block (medmc: "forthcoming", no citation published yet), and an explicit Launch button replacing the auto-redirect (removes "redirect anxiety"). medmc's container page got its own accent color (#5b4b8a, plum/indigo) distinct from medci's teal, scoped to the marketing page only -- the live Shiny UI stays teal. Then added real app screenshots (PRs #48-49), captured from the public standalone Connect Cloud URLs (share.connect.posit.cloud, no owner chrome) via html2canvas + a throwaway local upload server (no direct screenshot-to-disk tool available) -- see reference_connect_cloud_screenshot_capture memory. Noted in passing: medci's density plot threw a transient error on one cold navigation, then rendered fine on every reload after -- looks like a Connect Cloud free-tier idle-wake timeout, not a code regression; not investigated further. Site: https://data-wise.github.io/mediation-apps/. Separately: mediationverse's public README/DESCRIPTION were scrubbed to CRAN-published packages only (medfit, RMediation) -- see that repo's own .STATUS.
prior_done: 2026-08-04 (earlier same day) -- both medci and medmc first went LIVE on Connect Cloud (connect.posit.cloud), verified working. medci: root cause of 3 failed deploy attempts was Connect Cloud's native GitHub-connect flow cloning the raw repo tree directly (not an rsconnect bundle) with no renv support at all -- .Rprofile/renv/ removed entirely (PRs #11-16). Shipped UI modernization in three rounds (quick wins #1-5, medium wins #6-8, copy/download controls) plus a debounce fix for live-reactivity error-flashing, then a follow-up fix (adversarial review caught it) for a case where the plot output hadn't actually inherited the debounce and medci() was being computed twice per settle. medmc: migrated per SPEC-medmc-migration-2026-08-04.md -- not a straight port, since current RMediation::ci() is an S7 generic with no equivalent for the original's arbitrary-formula calling pattern. Reimplemented Monte Carlo + Asymptotic-Delta CI computation directly in the app, verified against the actual RMediation 1.1.3 source (contemporary with the 2014 original) after an adversarial spec review caught a point-estimate assumption error before implementation. Added a live matrix sanity-check swatch (PR #32) next to medmc's Variance-Covariance Matrix input -- renderUI CSS grid + magnitude-scaled PSD check, sourced from the existing parseSigma() reactive so it inherits validation and stays independent of the debounced results(); plan adversarially reviewed before implementation (abstract-weaving-boot.md). Follow-up UX batch (PRs #36-38, released to main via #39): renamed medmc's title panel to "Monte Carlo Confidence Intervals for Indirect Effects" with a one-line description; made the color-grid swatch opt-in (checkbox, default off -- it duplicated the numeric table without adding much) and blanked the redundant mirrored upper-triangle cells in the sanity-check table; replaced the Significance Level numericInput with a selectizeInput offering common presets (.0001/.005/.01/.05/.1) plus free-typed values validated against the open interval (0,1) -- this also caught and fixed a latent mixed-dependency bug where output$interval read input$alpha directly alongside the debounced results(), same bug class as medci's PR #27. PR #35 (numericInput spinner-arrow CSS fix) was superseded and closed unmerged once #38 replaced the widget entirely.
type: apps
last_updated: 2026-08-04 (session 2)

## mediation-apps

Sibling repo to the mediationverse package ecosystem, holding standalone
Shiny apps deployed to Posit Connect Cloud. Two apps live: medci
(confidence intervals for a two-coefficient indirect effect) and medmc
(Monte Carlo/Asymptotic-Delta CIs for an arbitrary user-formula), both
migrated from the legacy amplab shinyapps.io account and verified
working.

See CLAUDE.md for conventions; see mediationverse's
SPEC-shiny-apps-location-2026-08-03.md for the full design record.
